<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Fe de Nuevo México</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1598–1848</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Nuevo México</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Fe de Nuevo México was a province on the northern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-onate">Juan de Oñate</a>'s colonising expedition in 1598, with its capital at Santa Fe from about 1610. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-revolt">Pueblo Revolt</a> drove the Spanish out from 1680 to 1692. From 1776 it fell under the Commandancy General of the Internal Provinces; it became a territory of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1821, was occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1846 and ceded in 1848.</p></div>
